---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { contact } from '../content/site';

/**
 * Describes what this site actually does, not what a template says a site does.
 * Verified against the code on 13 Aug 2026:
 *
 *  - no analytics, no cookies, no tracking pixels, no third-party scripts
 *  - fonts are self-hosted, so a page load makes no external request at all
 *  - the only data collected is what someone types into one of the two forms
 *  - that data goes to Resend, which delivers it to Thread's inbox
 *
 * If any of those change — an analytics script, an embedded map, a hosted
 * video, a newsletter signup — this page has to change in the same commit.
 */
const updated = '13 August 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy · Thread"
  description="What Thread collects when you use this site, what happens to it, and how to have it removed. Short, because the site collects almost nothing."
>
  <Header />

  <section class="legal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>What this site collects.</h1>
      <div class="eyebrow">Privacy</div>
      <p class="lead" style="max-width:56ch">
        Almost nothing, and none of it automatically. This page says exactly what happens
        to the information you do send.
      </p>

      <h2>Visiting the site</h2>
      <p>
        There are no analytics, no cookies, no tracking pixels and no third-party scripts
        on this site. Typefaces are served from this domain rather than from a font
        service, so loading a page here makes no request to anyone else.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is hosted by Vercel. Like any web host, Vercel's servers handle the
        request and keep short-term operational logs, which can include your IP address
        and browser. Thread does not use those logs to build any profile of you.
      </p>

      <h2>Using one of the forms</h2>
      <p>
        The contact form and the systems map form collect only what you type into them:
        your name, your email address, and your answers to the questions on the form. There
        are no hidden fields beyond a single unused box that catches automated spam.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you submit, the contents are sent by email to Thread through Resend, an email
        delivery service, and land in Thread's ordinary email inbox. They are stored there
        like any other email.
      </p>

      <h2>What it's used for</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Replying to you</li>
        <li>Working on the thing you asked about</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        That is the whole list. Your details are not sold, not shared with anyone else, not
        used for advertising, and not added to a mailing list. There is no mailing list.
      </p>

      <h2>How long it's kept</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries are kept while the conversation is active and for as long as the work or
        the relationship is relevant afterwards. If you would rather they weren't, say so
        and they will be deleted.
      </p>

      <h2>Asking for a copy, a correction or a deletion</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> and ask. You do not
        need to explain why, and there is no form for it.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
      <p>
        If the site starts doing something it doesn’t do today, such as analytics, an
        embedded map or a newsletter, this page changes at the same time and the date
        below changes with it.
      </p>

      <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Base>
